      numberRoman: 'EPILOGUE',
      title: 'The Patience of Roots Against the Haste of Tenders',
      subtitle:
        'A watershed remembers whether we came to heal its soil and water—or merely to close a financial year.',
      dateline: 'AWANTIPORA · WULAR SHALLOWS · PIR PANJAL TREELINE · NOVEMBER 2026',
      paragraphs: [
        'In late autumn across the Kashmir Valley, the surface theatre of summer green fades, revealing the true architecture of the landscape. Along the Watlab and Bandipora shallows of Wular and the reed channels of Hokersar, early cohorts of migratory mallards, teal, and greylag geese circle downward, reading water depth, submerged *Potamogeton* beds, and mudflat contours with evolutionary precision that no contractor’s completion certificate can fool. Two thousand meters higher along the Pir Panjal and Sindh ridges, papery silver-white stems of *Betula utilis* stand leafless against November wind, their winter survival already decided underground by fungal hyphae, root starch reserves, and soil moisture stored months earlier.',
        'The International Conference on Nature-Based Solutions hosted by IUST at Awantipora in August 2026 rendered a lasting public service by placing those wetlands, floodplains, and mountain forests at the centre of Jammu & Kashmir’s climate-resilience and fiscal conversation. Now comes the harder test that no four-day conference can pass on its own: confronting the procurement machine waiting outside the university gate.',
        'If “Nature-Based Solutions” becomes merely a fashionable new budget header under which the same agencies pour concrete toe-walls, dig three-year *Robinia* pits, scrape Ramsar seed banks with heavy excavators, and sell unverified carbon offsets before vanishing in Year Four, we will have betrayed both fiscal prudence and Himalayan ecology under the banner of saving them.',
        'Nature does not bid on e-procurement portals, does not rush photosynthesis to meet a March 31 treasury deadline, and does not sign twelve-month defect-liability waivers. A floodplain marsh, a deodar rhizosphere, and a birch treeline will work tirelessly for Kashmir’s safety across centuries—but only when our laws, budgets, and institutions acquire the humility to match the twenty-year patience of roots.',
      ],
